import{_ as t,o as n,c as s,a2 as i}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 372 | Tang San vs. Gu Chensha: Differences Between Two Predatory Systems","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 372 | Tang San vs. Gu Chensha: Differences Between Two Predatory Systems","no":372,"module":2,"tags":["Dou Continent","Tang San","Gu Chensha","Dragon Talisman","Predatory-System Comparison","Comparison"],"related":["251-Protagonist-Uniqueness Standard","04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis","17-Plane Transcendent Standards"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0372_模块2-斗罗-唐三vs古尘沙-两种掠夺体系的差异.md","filePath":"en/0372_模块2-斗罗-唐三vs古尘沙-两种掠夺体系的差异.md"}'),a={name:"en/0372_模块2-斗罗-唐三vs古尘沙-两种掠夺体系的差异.md"};function o(r,e,l,h,g,u){return n(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<h1 id="entry-372-tang-san-vs-gu-chensha-differences-between-two-predatory-systems" tabindex="-1">Entry 372 | Tang San vs. Gu Chensha: Differences Between Two Predatory Systems <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-372-tang-san-vs-gu-chensha-differences-between-two-predatory-systems" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 372 | Tang San vs. Gu Chensha: Differences Between Two Predatory Systems&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dou Continent System Decomposition (Entry 13 · Comparison) | Benchmark base: Documents 251, 04, 17</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-one-grabs-stock-one-creates-increment" tabindex="-1">Introduction: One grabs stock, one creates increment <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-one-grabs-stock-one-creates-increment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: One grabs stock, one creates increment&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Gu Chensha (Dragon Talisman) and Tang San are two extremes of web-literature predatory systems: Gu Chensha is known for the single-log apex of &quot;bearing sins for all beings, casually creating universes&quot;; Tang San for systematic predation of &quot;hunting soul beasts, deifying the whole family.&quot; Their protagonist-uniqueness dependency differs — Gu Chensha is <strong>extreme (single-log)</strong>, Tang San is <strong>high (gift-style leaning oligarchic)</strong>. This entry, taking the law-first axiom as core, compares the texture difference between the two predatory systems. Protagonist uniqueness dependency: <strong>Tang San = high (gift-style leaning oligarchic)</strong>. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judging base has been upgraded to the six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Gu-Chensha-style waste</strong>: energy immense but all beings &quot;made dragons by him&quot;; everything credited to the single greatest person; civilization&#39;s self-organization ability atrophies</li><li><strong>Tang-San-style waste</strong>: energy limited but institutionalized; predation spread into every cultivator&#39;s daily routine; larger in scale, more hidden</li><li><strong>Difference</strong>: Gu Chensha is &quot;one person too strong so waste&quot;; Tang San is &quot;one system too bad so waste&quot;</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Gu-Chensha path</strong>: single-log — protagonist falls, all beings have no support</li><li><strong>Tang-San path</strong>: systemic — even if Tang San steps down, the soul-ring-hunting system still runs; regression is structural, not personal</li><li><strong>Conclusion</strong>: Tang-San-style regression is harder to fix than Gu-Chensha-style — because it grows in institutions</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Gu Chensha</strong>: predation in &quot;exclusive occupation of the apex&quot; — he admits all beings can become dragons, but the achievement depends entirely on his mercy</li><li><strong>Tang San</strong>: predation in &quot;killing to seize Origin&quot; — he shouts no grand slogans, yet writes predation into every level</li><li><strong>Hardness comparison</strong>: Tang San&#39;s predation is harder (irreversible killing); Gu Chensha&#39;s predation is softer (warm outer garment); but in structural damage, Tang San&#39;s institutional predation covers more ground</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Gu Chensha Single-Log</th><th>Tang San Systemic</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dependency</td><td>Extreme</td><td>High</td><td>Extremely low</td></tr><tr><td>Predation form</td><td>Exclusive apex</td><td>Institutional killing</td><td>Develop increment</td></tr><tr><td>Repair difficulty</td><td>Medium (topple one person)</td><td>High (must change institutions)</td><td>No repair needed</td></tr><tr><td>Way out</td><td>Together become dragons</td><td>Path D man-made Dao-Law rings</td><td>Myriad Ranks republicanism</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The alternative&#39;s crux: for Tang San, what needs changing is not the protagonist, but the institution itself.</p><p>For Tang-San-style systemic predation, Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s antidote is Path D · human-engineered Dao-Law soul rings and Lin Hao-style reconstruction: not hoping for a kinder protagonist, but directly changing institutions — rewriting &quot;every ring must be seized&quot; into &quot;Dao laws grow by themselves.&quot; Lin Hao, as a victim of old rules, proves institutional predation is not unchangeable, as long as someone is willing to turn from victim into rule-rewriter.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: juxtapose the two predatory systems</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: respectively inject &quot;change protagonist&quot; and &quot;change institution&quot; interventions</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: civilization regression rate</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output &quot;Single-Log vs. Systemic Predation Repair-Cost Comparison&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: low (Tang San)</strong>: Gu Chensha&#39;s worldview also late inflates, but Tang San retcons more frequently</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: extreme (Tang San)</strong></li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: Tang San = high; Gu Chensha = extreme</li></ul><p>The comparison between Tang San and Gu Chensha reveals the fate of two kinds of predation: Gu Chensha&#39;s single log, topple one person and it may be solved; Tang San&#39;s system, even with a new protagonist, still runs the same. The former&#39;s lesion is in the person, the latter&#39;s lesion is in the law — hence Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s diagnosis of Tang San is &quot;must change the operating system,&quot; not &quot;change to a better protagonist.&quot;</p><p>Tang-San-style system and Gu-Chensha-style single log also have a key difference: Gu Chensha at least admits all beings &quot;made dragons by him&quot;; his grand narrative still has all beings&#39; shadow; Tang San&#39;s system compresses all beings into hunt targets and backdrops. The former&#39;s problem is &quot;bearing on behalf of all beings&quot;; the latter&#39;s problem is &quot;consuming all beings to feed.&quot; Heng Yuan Zhou criticizes the latter more heavily, because it did not even reach the step of &quot;seeing all beings.&quot;</p><p>Tang-San-style system and Gu-Chensha-style single log can also be compared on &quot;all-being subjectivity&quot;: Gu Chensha bears sins for all beings, at least admits all beings are &quot;those on whose behalf sins are borne&quot;; in Tang San&#39;s system, soul beasts do not even qualify for &quot;sins borne on their behalf&quot;; they are merely consumed objects. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s demand of Tang San is therefore higher: not only must predation stop, but the consumed must be re-included as &quot;members with subjectivity.&quot; Gu Chensha&#39;s problem is overstepping his mandate; Tang San&#39;s problem is seeing as nothing — the latter is farther from Myriad Ranks republicanism.</p><p>Supplementary verdict: Tang-San-style system is harder to treat than Gu-Chensha-style single log, because the lesion is in the law, not the person. Gu Chensha topple one person and it may be solved; Tang San with a new protagonist still hunts. This is also why Heng Yuan Zhou strikes Tang San harder — what it requires is not a kinder protagonist, but an operating-system change. Lin Hao-style reconstructors&#39; value lies precisely in that he touches the law, not the person.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: one is waste from being too strong, one is waste from institutions</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: Tang San makes predation everyday and institutional</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang San is harder than Tang Luo, because Tang Luo at least did not make predation a universal procedure</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: Tang San&#39;s institutional predation harms the widest swathe of Myriad Ranks</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: both predations are extremely far from a symbiotic cosmos</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Gu Chensha&#39;s problem is &quot;one person bears too much&quot;; Tang San&#39;s problem is &quot;a bad system makes everyone grab.&quot; The former topple one person and it may be solved; the latter must be pulled up by the root — this is precisely what Path D and Lin Hao do.</p><p>In the final analysis, Tang San vs. Gu Chensha · differences between two predatory systems described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../模块2-诸天对标批判/259_模块2-唐罗-古尘沙对比篇.html">Entry 259 · Tang-Luo Gu-Chensha Comparison</a> · <a href="./376_模块2-斗罗-唐三vs衡元宙-魂环掠夺与人造道则的分野.html">Entry 376 · Tang San vs. Heng Yuan Zhou</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',30)])])}const m=t(a,[["render",o]]);export{c as __pageData,m as default};
